nio: do not wait for dlil threads before launchd

Run 590 got past waitForSystemMapper and into bsd_init.  The
board now stops at

    dlil_init: Waiting for all the create dlil kernel threads
               to get scheduled at least once.

A bounded wait was already added here, but its bound is in
msleep ticks, and the clock is not ticking this early in the
boot -- the same reason the IOBSD and mapper waits had to be
removed.  The first msleep never returns, so the five-slice
bound is never reached and bsd_init stops for good.

The network stack is not what the launchd handoff needs; the
comment in this very function says so.  Start with the wait
counter already at its bound: the loop is skipped, the pending
count is reported, and the boot carries on into the rest of
bsd_init.  The earlier VERIFY of the pending count is at the
top of this function, before any thread is created, so it is
unaffected.

diff --git a/bsd/net/dlil.c b/bsd/net/dlil.c
index 9e683da..8303f17 100644
--- a/bsd/net/dlil.c
+++ b/bsd/net/dlil.c
@@ -2719,7 +2719,12 @@ dlil_init(void)
 		 * report what is still pending and carry on: the rest of the network
 		 * stack is not what the launchd handoff needs.
 		 */
-		int nio_wait = 0;
+		/* nio: msleep's tick timeout never expires this early in the
+		 * boot (the clock is not ticking yet), so the bounded wait below
+		 * hangs on its first msleep and bsd_init stops here.  The network
+		 * stack is not needed to hand off to launchd; start already past
+		 * the loop so the count is reported and the boot carries on. */
+		int nio_wait = 5;
 		int nio_ts = 100;
 
 		while (dlil_pending_thread_cnt != 0 && nio_wait < 5) {
